    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipNumber`, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince the value is derived purely from the owner's own stored fields (like the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `householdId`), I exposed it as a read-time mapper derivation rather than a new DB column:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (generates the `OwnerDto` field).\n- **`MembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper following the `Household` pattern: `of(customerCode, registrationDate)` returns `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, year % 100)`, and returns `null` when either input is absent.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression for `membershipNumber` calling the helper.\n\nThe null-guard matters because the seed owners have no `customer_code`/`registration_date`, and the mapper is used by the GET/list endpoints too \u2014 without it those reads would NPE. New owners always get a `registrationDate` (defaulted in `BuildOwner`) and a `customerCode` (assigned in the pipeline), so their membership number is always populated.\n\nThe acceptance test and full suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
